Feature: Rank Product Performance by Revenue
  To increase revenue, we need to identify top-performing products by ranking them by revenue across different countries using a 12-month dataset.

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog as purgo_playground
    And the Unity Catalog Schema as information_schema
    And the table d_product_revenue exists in the schema

  Scenario: Capture product performance for Gold category
    Given the product type is specified as "ProductType"
    And the purchase date is the "PurchasedDate" column
    And we have a dataframe with revenue data over 12 months
    When the product is ranked among the top 3 for 6 or more months
    Then set the performance of "ProductType" to "Gold"

  Scenario: Capture product performance for Silver category
    Given the product type is specified as "ProductType"
    And the purchase date is the "PurchasedDate" column
    And we have a dataframe with revenue data over 12 months
    When the product is ranked among the top 3 for 3 to 5 months
    Then set the performance of "ProductType" to "Silver"

  Scenario: Capture product performance for Bronze category
    Given the product type is specified as "ProductType"
    And the purchase date is the "PurchasedDate" column
    And we have a dataframe with revenue data over 12 months
    When the product is ranked among the top 3 for less than 3 months
    Then set the performance of "ProductType" to "Bronze"

  Scenario: Error handling for missing product type
    Given the product type column is missing in the dataset
    When the process is executed
    Then an error occurs with message "Product type is required for ranking"

  Scenario: Error handling for incorrect purchased date format
    Given the purchased date column format is incorrect
    When the process is executed
    Then an error occurs with message "PurchasedDate should be in YYYY-MM-DD format"

  Scenario Outline: Validate product ranking by country
    Given the country is "<Country>"
    And the product type is "ProductType"
    When the dataframe is filtered by "<Country>"
    Then the rankings are adjusted correctly for "<Country>"

    Examples:
      | Country     |
      | USA         |
      | Canada      |
      | Germany     |
      | Australia   |
      | Japan       |

  Scenario Outline: Validate performance assignment over different months
    Given the <ProductType> has ranked in the top 3 for <Months> months
    When evaluating performance status
    Then the result should be "<Performance>"

    Examples:
      | ProductType | Months | Performance |
      | A           | 6      | Gold        |
      | B           | 4      | Silver      |
      | C           | 2      | Bronze      |
      | D           | 8      | Gold        |
